            "The Guaranteed Service Model, pioneered by Simpson in 1958 and modernized by Stephen Graves and Sean Willems in 2000, assumes that every stage in the supply chain quotes a deterministic, guaranteed service time to its downstream customer nodes. Under GSM, if Stage A quotes a guaranteed service time of two days to Stage B, Stage A commits to fulfilling all incoming orders from Stage B within exactly two days, one hundred percent of the time, provided incoming demand remains within a pre-defined bounded demand envelope.",
